Chapter: DeviceEffect

 The Device effect marks code that runs on a GPU. Functions with
 Device in their effect row are kernels (when the row has no host
 effects) or device functions (callable from kernels). The compiler
 emits PTX for any definition reachable from a Device-effected root.

 We say:

Section: Definitions

  effect Device where
    thread-idx-x : [Device] Integer
    thread-idx-y : [Device] Integer
    thread-idx-z : [Device] Integer
    block-idx-x  : [Device] Integer
    block-idx-y  : [Device] Integer
    block-idx-z  : [Device] Integer
    block-dim-x  : [Device] Integer
    block-dim-y  : [Device] Integer
    block-dim-z  : [Device] Integer
    grid-dim-x   : [Device] Integer
    grid-dim-y   : [Device] Integer
    grid-dim-z   : [Device] Integer
    sync-threads : [Device] Nothing
    device-load : Integer, Integer -> [Device] Integer
    device-store : Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Device] Integer
    device-load-f64 : Integer, Integer -> [Device] Real
    device-store-f64 : Integer, Integer, Real -> [Device] Integer

